<title>CANADA: Canada's Martin sees deficit at 1 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin sees deficit at 1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Finance Minister Paul Martin on Wednesday made the following forecasts in his autumn 1996 budget update (figures in billions of Canadian dollars):</p>
<p>				1995/96   1996/97   1997/98  1998/99</p>
<p>Revenues		     130.3  (R)133.5  (R)139.1	N/A</p>
<p>Program spending	   112.0  (R)108.8  (R)105.6	N/A</p>
<p>Public debt charges	 46.9  (R) 46.5  (R) 47.5	N/A</p>
<p>Underlying deficit    (R) 28.6	 21.8     14.0	N/A</p>
<p>Contingency reserve	  nil	 2.5	 3.0	N/A</p>
<p>Deficit		   (R) 28.6	24.3	17.0	N/A</p>
<p>Deficit as pct of GDP	3.7	 3.0	 2.0	1.0</p>
</text>
